#!/usr/bin/env bash
#
# Normalize PKGLIST package-administration files.
#
# Older versions of the build script's package_deb() saved package build
# numbers under a key with a doubled arch suffix (pkg_1.0_amd64_amd64)
# while looking them up under the single-arch key (pkg_1.0_amd64). That
# polluted the pkglist and, once both key forms existed, made the build
# number computation fail (the count was "incremented but not saved").
#
# This script rewrites each pkglist file so every key has the single arch
# suffix:
#   - doubled-arch keys are renamed to their single-arch form;
#   - if both forms exist for the same package, the highest count wins;
#   - duplicate keys are merged (highest count wins);
#   - broken entries with an empty count are kept (they are treated as 0).
#
# The rewrite is atomic (write to .tmp, then rename) and idempotent, so it
# is safe to run repeatedly.
#
# Copyright 2011-2026 Mark Verboom
#
